        "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21835961",
        "metadata": {
          "title": "Topological Quantization of Mathematical Structures (TQMS)",
          "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21835961",
          "publication_date": "2026-08-07",
          "description": "<p class=\"15\"><span>This paper introduces the theoretical framework of Topological Quantization of Mathematical Structures (TQMS), a novel paradigm that bridges continuous abstract spaces and discrete algebraic invariants. The core philosophy of TQMS rests on the systematic mapping of general mathematical structures into discrete quantities, denoted as Q(X), thereby translating continuous structural variations into distinct quantum-like spectral shifts. By establishing a rigorous quantization operator, we investigate the underlying phenomena of structural mutations, topological phase transitions, and discrete deformations within abstract spaces. Furthermore, this framework yields a new class of invariant theories that extend traditional topological and algebraic classifications. We present the foundational axioms, construct the operator mechanics, analyze structural quantization phenomena, and outline prospective directions for abstract structural analysis without relying on empirical or experimental validations, keeping the discourse purely within theoretical mathematics.</span></p>",
